It contains no third-party source code. The statistical methods it implements
(Probabilistic Sharpe Ratio, Minimum Track Record Length, Deflated Sharpe Ratio,
Probability of Backtest Overfitting via CSCV, the multiple-testing haircut, and the
Lo (2002) autocorrelation adjustment) are re-implemented from the published papers
cited in docs/CHECKS.md. The NYSE trading calendar rules are written from the
exchange's published holiday rules. The BYMA holiday list (2015-2026) is a compilation
of public dates; the source and verification status of each date are documented in
docs/CALENDAR_BYMA.md, and partially or not verified dates must be checked against the
official BYMA calendar before use.

empyrical-reloaded (Apache-2.0) is used only as an independent test oracle in the
development dependencies; it is not imported at runtime and not redistributed.
